From 07b4ac68dd94a125f15bf6d2b0d16b433bb851e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:32:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] firmware: qcom: pas_tee: clear the metadata pointer on
 release

qcom_pas_start() releases the image metadata once auth_and_reset() has
succeeded, and qcom_pas_unprepare() releases it again when the remote
processor is stopped. qcom_pas_metadata_release() skips a context whose
ptr is NULL, which the SCM backend relies on, but the TEE backend frees
the shared memory and leaves ptr set. Stopping a remote processor that
was started therefore frees it twice:

  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000004 [#1]  SMP
  pc : tee_shm_put+0x20/0x1b0
  lr : tee_shm_free+0x10/0x20
  Call trace:
   tee_shm_put+0x20/0x1b0 (P)
   tee_shm_free+0x10/0x20
   qcom_pas_tee_metadata_release+0x14/0x20
   qcom_pas_metadata_release+0x34/0x44
   qcom_pas_unprepare+0x1c/0x5c
   rproc_shutdown+0xe0/0x150
   state_store+0xb8/0x100

Clear ptr after freeing the shared memory, as the SCM backend does.

Fixes: 1cd5c61959bd ("firmware: qcom: Add a PAS TEE service")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_pas_tee.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_pas_tee.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_pas_tee.c
index af73d0a68525..dcb3c9ef2a7c 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_pas_tee.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_pas_tee.c
@@ -389,6 +389,7 @@ static void qcom_pas_tee_metadata_release(struct device *dev,
 	struct tee_shm *mdata_shm = ctx->ptr;
 
 	tee_shm_free(mdata_shm);
+	ctx->ptr = NULL;
 }
 
 static struct qcom_pas_ops qcom_pas_ops_tee = {
